2. INTERPRETATION
lower envelope=four-sector composition around a directed edge; it is local equinumerosity/equidistribution only
upper envelope=four-sector deck plus both endpoint-deletion children; it is the safe local two-ended witness
A000568(n+1)=global tournament classes; it sits between as a global-consistency quotient of local edge witnesses
LRC translation: raw scalar/SPEC sectors are too coarse, full edge packets are deliberately overcomplete, and the proof certificate should be the quotient where local edge witnesses glue globally without losing the LRC predicate.

3. TOURNAMENT ANALYSIS OVER QUOTIENT CARRIERS
vertices=proof carriers / quotient operators, not runners or scalar counts
pairwise_observable=majority over axes a000568_wedge_explains,lrc_predicate_retention,controlled_forgetting,tail_tip_payload,global_gluing,spec_floor_transfer,finite_checkability,failure_guard
switch=A->B when A wins more axes; ties use global_consistency_quotient -> paired_tail_tip_child_envelope -> A000568_middle_orbit_count -> observer_extension_cut_payload -> resonance_lattice_SPEC_certificate -> edge_floor_packet_schema -> asano_lee_yang_dichotomy -> raw_four_sector_composition -> raw_count_numerology
